WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.838
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:09.269
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:16.029
Unit sixteen: Safety at Home. In this unit, you will talk about staying safe at home.

4
00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:17.878
Safe.

5
00:00:18.578 --> 00:00:20.624
Safe means not in danger.

6
00:00:20.924 --> 00:00:22.460
Stay safe at home.

7
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.777
Your turn. Say: Safe.

8
00:00:28.477 --> 00:00:29.281
Safe.

9
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:30.994
Knife.

10
00:00:31.694 --> 00:00:33.856
Knife means a sharp tool for cutting.

11
00:00:34.156 --> 00:00:35.517
Don't touch the knife.

12
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:39.288
Your turn. Say: Knife.

13
00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:42.582
Knife.

14
00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:44.364
Fire.

15
00:00:45.064 --> 00:00:48.166
Fire means hot, bright flames that burn.

16
00:00:48.466 --> 00:00:50.895
Fire is very dangerous.

17
00:00:51.595 --> 00:00:54.167
Your turn. Say: Fire.

18
00:00:56.867 --> 00:00:57.717
Fire.

19
00:00:58.717 --> 00:00:59.648
Stove.

20
00:01:00.348 --> 00:01:02.777
Stove means the thing in the kitchen we cook on.

21
00:01:03.077 --> 00:01:04.508
The stove is hot.

22
00:01:05.208 --> 00:01:07.965
Your turn. Say: Stove.

23
00:01:10.665 --> 00:01:11.317
Stove.

24
00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:13.202
Medicine.

25
00:01:13.902 --> 00:01:16.458
Medicine means something you take when you are sick.

26
00:01:16.758 --> 00:01:19.002
Only take medicine from an adult.

27
00:01:19.702 --> 00:01:22.633
Your turn. Say: Medicine.

28
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:26.195
Medicine.

29
00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:28.614
Electricity.

30
00:01:29.314 --> 00:01:33.206
Electricity means the power that makes lights and machines work.

31
00:01:33.506 --> 00:01:35.227
Don't play with electricity.

32
00:01:35.927 --> 00:01:38.823
Your turn. Say: Electricity.

33
00:01:41.523 --> 00:01:42.652
Electricity.

34
00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:44.535
Careful.

35
00:01:45.235 --> 00:01:48.674
Careful means thinking about danger and avoiding it.

36
00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:50.718
Be careful on the stairs.

37
00:01:51.418 --> 00:01:54.094
Your turn. Say: Careful.

38
00:01:56.794 --> 00:01:57.656
Careful.

39
00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.489
Adult.

40
00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:02.130
Adult means a grown-up person.

41
00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.023
Ask an adult for help.

42
00:02:04.723 --> 00:02:07.480
Your turn. Say: Adult.

43
00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:11.030
Adult.

44
00:02:12.017 --> 00:02:14.202
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:14.502 --> 00:02:17.140
Rithy, what is dangerous in the kitchen?

46
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.274
The stove and the knife are dangerous.

47
00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:24.002
What should you remember?

48
00:02:25.317 --> 00:02:28.190
Don't touch the stove. Don't play with the knife.

49
00:02:29.483 --> 00:02:30.937
And if you feel sick?

50
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:35.251
Don't take medicine alone. Ask an adult.

51
00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.281
Grammar focus: Don't plus verb.

52
00:02:39.581 --> 00:02:42.431
Don't touch the stove. Don't play with fire.

53
00:02:42.731 --> 00:02:46.170
Use 'Don't' + verb to warn someone about danger.

54
00:02:47.183 --> 00:02:49.824
Now read and listen. Careful at Home.

55
00:02:50.124 --> 00:02:53.552
Home is a happy place, but we must be careful.

56
00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:57.128
I don't touch the knife or the hot stove.

57
00:02:58.417 --> 00:03:00.973
I never play with fire or electricity.

58
00:03:02.283 --> 00:03:04.701
I only take medicine from an adult.

59
00:03:06.017 --> 00:03:09.038
If something is dangerous, I tell an adult at once.

60
00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:13.049
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:13.349 --> 00:03:15.372
blank touch the hot stove!

62
00:03:15.672 --> 00:03:19.302
A, Don't. B, Doesn't. C, Not.

63
00:03:23.317 --> 00:03:25.026
The answer is A: Don't.

64
00:03:26.517 --> 00:03:28.795
A sharp tool for cutting is a blank.

65
00:03:29.095 --> 00:03:32.621
A, knife. B, stove. C, fire.

66
00:03:36.617 --> 00:03:38.872
The answer is A: knife.

67
00:03:40.383 --> 00:03:42.418
Only take medicine from an blank.

68
00:03:42.718 --> 00:03:47.091
A, adult. B, animal. C, friend.

69
00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:52.746
The answer is A: adult.

70
00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:58.330
Now it's your turn to speak. What should children be careful of at home?

71
00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:09.383
Children should be careful of the stove and knives. Don't play with fire, and ask an adult for help.

72
00:04:09.683 --> 00:04:11.357
Excellent answer, Rithy!

73
00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:16.674
Great work today! You learned eight new words and don't plus verb.

74
00:04:16.974 --> 00:04:21.322
Today's value is safety. Be careful near cars and roads.

75
00:04:21.622 --> 00:04:24.599
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:24.899 --> 00:04:27.992
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

